<span id="A3.T5.2.1.2.1.1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T5.2.1.2.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">STEP 1: Let’s identify each point in the image one by one.
<br class="ltx_break">- Red star: x=7, y=7
<br class="ltx_break">- Red circle: x=7, y=7
<br class="ltx_break">- Orange circle: x=6, y=7
<br class="ltx_break">- Green square: x=4, y=7
<br class="ltx_break">- Green triangle: x=3, y=5
<br class="ltx_break">- Blue square: x=1, y=3
<br class="ltx_break">- Blue triangle: x=1, y=3
<br class="ltx_break">- Orange star: x=6, y=1
<br class="ltx_break">STEP 2: **State the color and shape of the data point with the smallest x-value**
<br class="ltx_break">BE CONCISE; ONLY RESPOND WITH THE ANSWER. The color and shape of the data point with the smallest x-value =

<br class="ltx_break"></span></span>
</span>
</span></td></tr>
