<span id="A3.T11.2.3.3.1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T11.2.3.3.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Model response</span>: **Step 1: Identify the data points in the scatter plot.**</span>
<span id="A3.T11.2.3.3.1.3" class="ltx_p">The scatter plot displays 12 data points, each represented by a different color and shape (circle, triangle, square, or star). The colors are red, green, blue, and orange.</span>
<span id="A3.T11.2.3.3.1.4" class="ltx_p">**Step 2: Determine the y-values for each data point.**</span>
<span id="A3.T11.2.3.3.1.5" class="ltx_p">The y-values for each data point are as follows:</span>
<span id="A3.T11.2.3.3.1.6" class="ltx_p">* Red circle: 6.5
* Red triangle: 4.5
* Red square: 3.5
* Red star: 7.5
* Green circle: 2.5
* Green triangle: 1.5
* Green square: 4.5
* Green star: 2.5
* Blue circle: 4.5
* Blue triangle: 3.5
* Blue square: 2.5
* Orange circle: 1.5</span>
<span id="A3.T11.2.3.3.1.7" class="ltx_p">**Step 3: Identify the data point with the largest y-value.**</span>
<span id="A3.T11.2.3.3.1.8" class="ltx_p">The data point with the largest y-value is the red star, with a y-value of 7.5.</span>
<span id="A3.T11.2.3.3.1.9" class="ltx_p">**Answer:** The data point with the largest y-value is the <span id="A3.T11.2.3.3.1.9.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#E13B3B;">red star</span>.</span>
